---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, operator } from "../site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who publishes Creator Growth Tools, what it covers, and how it is funded.">
  <section class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A small, deliberately narrow review site.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      {site.name} publishes comparisons of the software creators and one-person businesses actually
      pay for. It is written for someone mid-decision who wants the trade-offs stated plainly and
      the sources shown.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is published by <a href={operator.url} rel="noopener">{operator.name}</a>, an
        independent one-person studio based in {operator.location} that builds small AI and
        automation tooling. There is no editorial team and no outside investor. Reaching the person
        who writes these pages takes one email: <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
      <p>
        We separate verified vendor facts from editorial assessment, and every article states which
        it is built on using a visible evidence grade. If we have not used a product first-hand, we
        do not claim hands-on testing or personal experience — see
        <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a> for what each grade requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Current scope</h2>
      <p>
        We cover newsletter, email marketing, and audience growth tools for creators and one-person
        businesses today, and we are extending into faceless creation, AI video, and AI voice
        tooling. <a href="/topics/">Topics</a> lists what is published and what is still planned,
        with planned topics marked as planned rather than filled with thin pages. We would rather
        keep a small number of comparisons verified than run a catalog we cannot maintain.
      </p>

      <h2>How this site is funded</h2>
      <p>
        Some outbound links are affiliate links, and every link is labeled on the page so you can
        see which is which before you click. Links that are not affiliate links earn us nothing, and
        a page with no affiliate link says exactly that. Affiliate relationships never decide which
        tool we recommend; see our <a href="/editorial-methodology/">editorial methodology</a> and
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How AI is used here</h2>
      <p>
        {operator.name} builds AI tooling, and AI assists the production of these pages — drafting,
        structuring, and checking consistency. It is not used to invent experience, sources, prices,
        screenshots, or results. Every factual claim traces to an official vendor page or verified
        public review consensus, a human decides every verdict, and the evidence grade on each
        article is the record of that boundary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
